    "level": "beginner",
    "tier": "secondary",
    "locale": "en",
    "sourceLocale": "fr",
    "translationStatus": "machine",
    "content": "Short answer\nBitcoin Core developers can be funded by grants, donations or independent companies. Funding does not grant the power to impose a new rule on the network.\n\nExplanation\n- Bitcoin Core does not sell a classic proprietary piece of software.\n- Developers can be funded by different organizations.\n- Diversity of funding reduces some risks of capture.\n- Sustainable funding remains a challenge for critical open-source software.\n\nLimits and confusions\nDiverse backing can reduce some risks of dependence without guaranteeing the absence of influence.",
