    "content": "Short answer\nMaintainers notably handle merging contributions into the Bitcoin Core repository. Users always choose which software and which rules they run.\n\nExplanation\n- Anyone can clone the repository and create a fork.\n- Maintainers have a practical merging role, not the power to change the rules accepted by users.\n- Pull requests can wait a long time for lack of qualified review.\n- If the focal point becomes untrustworthy, another focal point can emerge.\n\nLimits and confusions\nThe ability to create a software fork guarantees neither its adoption nor its security.",
