    "sourceLocale": "fr",
    "translationStatus": "machine",
    "content": "Short answer\nThe mining cost indicates the profitability of a given operation, not a guaranteed price floor for bitcoin.\n\nExplanation\n- When the price no longer covers an operation's costs, that operation can reduce or stop production.\n- The difficulty adjustment then changes mining competition; it does not force BTC buyers to pay a minimum price.\n\nLimits and confusions\nCosts and price can diverge; estimates from one group of miners do not represent the whole network.",
