    "content": "Short answer\nBitcoins that move after a long period of inactivity may correspond to a sale, but also to a wallet migration, an inheritance or a simple reorganization of funds.\n\nExplanation\n- An address waking up does not automatically mean a sale: it can be an internal transfer, a technical migration, a payment, an inheritance, a key recovery or profit-taking.\n- Analysis must distinguish the destination, change, dust, exchange labels and the later path of the UTXOs.\n- Very old BTC that move are often read as a market signal, but that reading remains probabilistic.\n\nLimits and confusions\nAge and on-chain movement alone prove neither identity nor intent.",
