    "locale": "en",
    "sourceLocale": "fr",
    "translationStatus": "machine",
    "content": "Short answer\nCoin clipping consists of removing part of the precious metal while trying to keep the coin's face value.\n\nExplanation\n- It is a historical form of devaluation and monetary fraud.\n- It shows the difference between face value and real content.\n- Authorities as well as individuals can have an incentive to tamper with money.\n- Bitcoin makes the supply verifiable through consensus rules rather than through physical weight.\n\nLimits and confusions\nPhysical clipping, the official alteration of metal content and a fall in the exchange rate are different mechanisms; comparing them must not blur them together.",
