    "sourceLocale": "fr",
    "translationStatus": "machine",
    "content": "Short answer\nDollarization is the use of the US dollar, officially or informally, in place of or alongside a weakened local currency. It often appears after high inflation, a crisis of confidence or hyperinflation.\n\nExplanation\n- It can stabilize prices by importing a more credible currency.\n- It reduces the monetary sovereignty of the local state.\n- It can be official, or spontaneous on the part of private actors.\n- Bitcoin can be compared to an alternative form of voluntary currency substitution.\n\nLimits and confusions\nStability against the dollar does not guarantee constant purchasing power. Stablecoins add issuer, reserve, network and conversion risks.",
