    "locale": "en",
    "sourceLocale": "fr",
    "translationStatus": "machine",
    "content": "Short answer\nFree banking refers to a system in which competing banks issue means of payment under common rules, without a central bank's monopoly on issuance. Its supporters expect discipline to be exerted by customers and by the other banks.\n\nExplanation\n- The possibility of conversion and trust in the issuer play a central role.\n- Free banking models and their historical experiments are not all identical.\n- Competition between banks and Bitcoin's issuance rules are distinct mechanisms.\n\nLimits and confusions\nThe benefits of competition are a thesis defended by this school of thought. They are not a guarantee against panics, fraud or liquidity failures.",
