    "content": "Short answer\nMonetary debasement consists of reducing the quantity or quality of precious metal in a currency while maintaining its nominal value.\n\nExplanation\n- It creates a gap between legal value and real value.\n- It often triggers hoarding of the good coins and circulation of the bad ones.\n- It can lead to rising prices, loss of confidence and disruption of economic calculation.\n\nLimits and confusions\nAltering the metal content is not synonymous with an exchange-rate devaluation or an automatic, proportional rise in prices.",
