    "locale": "en",
    "sourceLocale": "fr",
    "translationStatus": "machine",
    "content": "Short answer\nThe stock-to-flow ratio compares the existing stock of a good to its annual production, and measures how hard it is to dilute the existing supply.\n\nExplanation\n- Gold keeps a high ratio because it is accumulated and little consumed.\n- Metals that are rarer in annual production can be less monetary if their stock is small or quickly consumed.\n- The ratio helps in understanding monetary scarcity, store of value and competition between monetary goods.\n\nLimits and confusions\nThis relationship between stock and flow does not account for all of demand and is not a law of price formation. It cannot guarantee a future price for Bitcoin.",
