    "locale": "en",
    "sourceLocale": "fr",
    "translationStatus": "machine",
    "content": "Short answer\nChain split risk appears when nodes or miners apply incompatible rules and extend different branches of the blockchain.\n\nExplanation\n- A split can be caused by a bug, a poorly coordinated upgrade or a social disagreement.\n- Users, exchanges and wallets may see misleading confirmations during the incident.\n- The severity depends on hashrate, on the economy and on how long the divergence lasts.\n- Preserving consensus harmony is a priority of Bitcoin upgrades.\n\nLimits and confusions\nA temporary divergence does not necessarily imply the lasting creation of 2 assets.",
