    "content": "Short answer\nThe first known Bitcoin transaction between 2 people took place on 2009-01-12, when Satoshi Nakamoto sent 10 BTC to Hal Finney. It marks Bitcoin's passage from launched software to a network in use.\n\nExplanation\n- Hal Finney is the first known recipient of a Bitcoin transaction.\n- The transaction concretely tested the peer-to-peer sending described in the whitepaper.\n- It links Satoshi and Finney in the network's first days.\n- It has become a major historical landmark.\n\nLimits and confusions\nThis is the first known transfer between people, distinct from the first coinbase transaction.",
