    "translationStatus": "machine",
    "content": "Short answer\nBitcoin discretion consists of limiting what you reveal publicly about your holdings, wallets, habits, addresses, storage locations and security practices. It protects both digital privacy and physical security.\n\nExplanation\n- Talking publicly about amounts held increases social and physical risk.\n- Photos, talks, social networks and informal conversations can create exploitable signals.\n- Discretion does not prevent education; it separates teaching from personal exposure.\n- It complements KYC minimization, OPSEC and physical security.\n\nLimits and confusions\nDiscretion reduces some exposure without eliminating physical risks or traces that are already public.",
