    "sourceLocale": "fr",
    "translationStatus": "machine",
    "content": "Short answer\nData breach monitoring consists of checking whether an email or identifier appears in compromised databases, then prioritizing password rotation and enabling additional protections.\n\nExplanation\n- An email present in a breach increases the risk of targeted phishing.\n- Reused passwords turn a minor breach into a chain of compromises.\n- Breach alerts call for a password change and a review of active sessions.\n- Monitoring does not replace prevention; unique passwords and 2FA remain essential.\n\nLimits and confusions\nThe absence of an alert does not prove the absence of a breach; a seed or private key is never submitted to a lookup service.",
