    "content": "Short answer\nDigital hygiene is the set of simple, repeatable habits that reduce exposure to common attacks: unique passwords, 2FA, updates, backups, caution with links and separating uses.\n\nExplanation\n- Seeking perfect security is unrealistic; the goal is to reduce the most likely risks.\n- Progress works best in stages: secure email, password manager, 2FA, backups, browser and network.\n- Tools do not replace behavior: checking the URL, the sender, where software comes from and unusual requests.\n- For a bitcoiner, this foundation also protects exchange accounts, cloud access, public content and recovery procedures.\n\nLimits and confusions\nA routine reduces frequent risks without guaranteeing that a device is clean.",
