    "level": "beginner",
    "tier": "secondary",
    "locale": "en",
    "sourceLocale": "fr",
    "translationStatus": "machine",
    "content": "Short answer\nExtensions can access pages and data according to their permissions; a compromised extension can therefore expose accounts or payments.\n\nExplanation\n- Permissions can allow reading or modifying certain pages, or even access to sensitive data.\n- A useful extension is still a software dependency to reassess after an update, a change of owner or unusual behavior.\n\nLimits and confusions\nLimiting extensions and their rights does not mean that every password manager or autofill tool is to be avoided.",
