    "sourceLocale": "fr",
    "translationStatus": "machine",
    "content": "Short answer\nPrivate mode mainly limits the local traces of a session: history, persistent cookies and forms. It does not make you anonymous to the ISP, the site visited or a corporate network.\n\nExplanation\n- Useful for temporary sessions, one-off searches or avoiding certain persistent cookies.\n- It does not hide the IP address or network activity.\n- It does not protect against malware, phishing or fake sites.\n- It is best explained as a tool for reducing local traces, not as Tor.\n\nLimits and confusions\nPrivate mode does not hide the IP address. Downloaded files and the traces kept by services or the network do not disappear when the window is closed.",
    "parentIds": [
      "non-blockchain-privacy-leaks",
      "tor-browser"
    ],
    "relatedIds": [
      "non-blockchain-privacy-leaks",
      "tor-browser"
    ],
    "reviewMethod": "semantic_light",
    "sources": [
      "PlanB scu101 — Update Your Online Security"
    ],
    "questions": [
      "The limits of private browsing — what is the mechanism and what are its limits?"
    ],
