    "sourceLocale": "fr",
    "translationStatus": "machine",
    "content": "Short answer\nA so-called algorithmic stablecoin aims at a peg through issuance rules, burning rules or market incentives rather than a simple full reserve in the target currency.\n\nExplanation\n- The peg depends in particular on liquidity and on confidence in the mechanism.\n- A drop in confidence can trigger chain reactions and a loss of the peg.\n- The real collateral and the exit options need to be examined, not just the algorithmic label.\n\nLimits and confusions\nThe mechanisms differ between purely algorithmic, crypto-collateralized and hybrid models. An issuance rule does not guarantee the value on the market.",
