    "content": "Short answer\nStablecoins can be used to transfer value denominated in a currency, to receive payments or to hold a unit of account temporarily. They retain the risks tied to their issuer or to their backing mechanism.\n\nExplanation\n- An international transfer still depends on access to on-ramps and off-ramps.\n- A digital dollar unit can make some payments easier without removing the exchange-rate risk against local expenses.\n- Payments and treasury are possible uses, not investment recommendations.\n\nLimits and confusions\nPossible uses prove neither measured adoption nor guaranteed protection. Costs, access to conversion, applicable law and freezing risk depend on the context.",
