    "locale": "en",
    "sourceLocale": "fr",
    "translationStatus": "machine",
    "content": "Short answer\nIn March 2023, USDC temporarily lost its peg after a reserve exposure to Silicon Valley Bank was revealed, before returning toward 1 dollar after public intervention.\n\nExplanation\n- It shows that a fiat-backed stablecoin also depends on the traditional banking system.\n- The market quickly prices in reserve risk.\n- The FDIC/Fed intervention limited the loss in this case.\n- A reputable stablecoin can still suffer a crisis of confidence.\n\nLimits and confusions\nThis is a historical episode from March 2023, not a description of current reserves. The return to the peg in this case does not guarantee the outcome of a future crisis.",
